Worktree Session includes implementation and interaction ideas adapted from:

  dsh-git-worktree
  https://github.com/LaoYueHanNi/dsh-git-worktree
  Commit reviewed: 7eaefe0bc70d5b8001403a162fa0bd7d65fe5aa2
  License: MIT

The adapted concepts are limited to the DSH bundle/client declaration pattern,
conversation.input.left placement, same-origin Host route shape, local Git ref
discovery, and registering a Git worktree as a DSH Workspace. Worktree Session
uses a new base-ref/first-submit transaction, unique task branches, durable
operation metadata, dependency/environment preparation, and conservative
handoff/cleanup rules. It does not copy the reference plugin's in-place branch
switch or branch-reuse behavior.

